View before: [apple, banana, cherry]
View after modifying the array directly: [avocado, banana, cherry]
Caught: UnsupportedOperationException -- Arrays.asList() does not support add()/remove()
Independent ArrayList (add() works): [avocado, banana, cherry, date]
List.toArray(new String[0]): [avocado, banana, cherry, date]

Array: fixed size, can hold primitives, index access is the fastest option.
List (e.g. ArrayList): resizable, only reference types, richer API.
